================================================================================
PREAMBLE
================================================================================

This License governs the DLEPS platform (Deep Learning based Efficacy Prediction
System for drug discovery), including its source code, model weights, and any
associated documentation, data samples, and interfaces (collectively, the
"Software").

The Software was developed for academic and non-profit research purposes. It
predicts the therapeutic efficacy of small molecules from transcriptional
profiles and molecular structure. The Licensor grants permission to use the
Software strictly within that academic research envelope, and deliberately
withholds permission for any commercial exploitation — including commercial
exploitation of the predictions the Software itself produces.

The parties intend this License to be read as a whole. Where a restriction is
expressed in more than one section, the more restrictive reading applies.


================================================================================
1. DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

1.1 "Software" means all source code, model weights (including the Molecular
    VAE, the DLEPS dense/transformer prediction heads, and the auxiliary
    logP, toxicity and ADMET models distributed under the `data/` directory
    and their derivatives), scripts, configuration files, container images,
    APIs, client and server components, documentation, and sample data made
    available in connection with the DLEPS project.

1.2 "Outputs" means any result produced by executing the Software, including
    but not limited to:
      (a) predicted efficacy, potency, connectivity/enrichment scores, or
          predicted therapeutic direction (e.g. disease-mimicking vs.
          disease-reversing) for any small molecule;
      (b) rankings, rankings-derived orderings, or hit lists of compounds;
      (c) predictions of ADMET, toxicity, logP, or solubility derived from
          the auxiliary models included in the Software;
      (d) any model, classifier, filter, or pipeline that is trained,
          fine-tuned, calibrated, initialized from, or otherwise derived from
          the Software or its Model Weights (a "Derived Model");
      (e) any dataset, table, figure, report, or database assembled from the
          foregoing.

1.3 "Academic Research" means use undertaken by, or on behalf of, a
    university, research institute, hospital, government laboratory, or
    non-profit research organization, for research, teaching, scholarly
    publication, or thesis/dissertation purposes, where the primary purpose of
    the activity is scientific investigation and not commercial exploitation.

1.4 "Commercial Use" means any use that is directed toward, or that directly
    or indirectly serves, a commercial purpose or the generation of revenue,
    including without limitation:
      (a) use within, or for the benefit of, a for-profit company,
          pharmaceutical or biotechnology enterprise, contract research
          organization, venture-backed entity, or any other profit-seeking
          legal person;
      (b) use to develop, screen, select, prioritize, or advance a compound,
          target, therapeutic hypothesis, or pipeline for commercial
          exploitation;
      (c) use to support a business activity, including but not limited to
          in-licensing, out-licensing, virtual screening campaigns,
          lead-optimization programs, due diligence, or investor materials;
      (d) use within any product or service offered for money, subscription,
          or other consideration;
      (e) use of the Outputs, or of any Derived Model, for any of the above.

1.5 "Licensor" means the copyright holder(s) identified in the header of this
    License, acting through the contact address given in Section 12.

1.6 "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising the permissions
    granted under Section 2.


