3. RESTRICTIONS ON USE
================================================================================

3.1 NO COMMERCIAL USE OF THE SOFTWARE.
    You may not use the Software, in whole or in part, for any Commercial Use.
    This restriction applies to the source code, the model weights, the
    services and interfaces, and any Derivative thereof, irrespective of
    whether such use is for a fee, is internally profitable, is performed for
    a client, or is cost-subsidized by a commercial entity.

3.2 NO COMMERCIAL USE OF THE OUTPUTS.
    Outputs shall be treated as Confidential Academic Results and are likewise
    subject to the Academic Research limitation. You may not use, disclose,
    publish, license, sell, or otherwise exploit any Output for any Commercial
    Use. For the avoidance of doubt, and without limitation:
      (a) an efficacy, potency, or connectivity prediction for a small
          molecule produced by running the Software may not be used to
          select, advance, justify, price, or promote a compound in a
          commercial context, nor may it be used in a regulatory submission,
          a due-diligence report, or an investor or commercial partner
          presentation;
      (b) a compound list, ranking, or hit list generated with the Software
          may not be transferred to, or used on behalf of, a commercial party;
      (c) a Derived Model, or a prediction produced by a Derived Model, is
          subject to this Section to the same extent as the original
          Software and Outputs.

    For the avoidance of doubt, this Section 3.2 does not restrict the
    publication of academic findings in scholarly journals, preprints,
    conference proceedings, or theses, provided that the Software is
    acknowledged in accordance with Section 4.4.

3.3 NO SUBLICENSING OR REDISTRIBUTION.
    You may not sublicense, rent, lease, host as a paid service, or otherwise
    make the Software or the Model Weights available to third parties except
    as expressly permitted by Section 2(e) for Academic Research.

3.4 NO REMOVAL OF NOTICES.
    You may not remove, alter, or obscure any copyright, authorship,
    attribution, license, or disclaimer notice in the Software, in the
    accompanying documentation, or in the Outputs, nor may You present
    Yourself as the author or owner of the Software.

3.5 NO REPRESENTATIONS OF ENDORSEMENT.
    You may not state or imply that the Licensor endorses, supports, or
    approves Your use of the Software, or that any prediction produced by the
    Software is endorsed or clinically validated by the Licensor.

3.6 COMPLIANCE WITH APPLICABLE LAW.
    Nothing in this License grants permission to use the Software in
    violation of applicable law, including export control, sanctions, and
    intellectual property law, or in a manner that would infringe the
    intellectual property rights of third parties.


